o her gardening.<br /> <br /> Speaking of <i>kalif</i>, of course the <b>Banu Haqim</b> know about growing weed with vitae, too. It\u2019s probable that there is more <b>Dur-An-Ki </b>alchemy happening like that.<br /> <br /> Disappointingly, I could find very little about <b>Lhiannan</b> horticulture. <b>Ogham</b> can animate plants with vitae, but is more focused on Names later on.<br /> <br /> Next, there are the <b>Lhaka</b> (Bahari vampires), who cultivate allegorical as well as real gardens as part of their devotion to Lilith. The <i>Guide to the Tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra</i> gives us the Nightshade <b>Necromancy</b> Path, for fruit that gives Deathsight and the creation of plant zombies.<br /> The same book also has a <b>Vicissitude</b> power that, by pouring vitae into soil, warps plants and enables fruit to ghoul those who eat it. Enoch has the Gardens of Malkav, in which the <b>Rafastio</b> experiment with ghouling plants. The book says they only had success with carnivorous plants, which is mighty silly (except for trapping mechanisms they are no different from other plants), so I\u2019m reading it as fungi, which are at least decomposers.<br /> <br /> And taking a peek outside, V:tR has ghouled plants as <i>Mandragora</i>, which can produce a substance called Lacrima. It\u2019s basically a drug for vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> From the above examples, a few commonalities can be gleamed:<br /> <br /> - Plants need to be fed with vitae. Usually, small amounts are sufficient, but doing it right is a learned ability. Just pouring some vitae on the soil does not work. Sometimes, the soil is enriched with corpses, or even the ashes of a slain vampire.<br /> <br /> - Botanical drugs or poisons can be enhanced in potency to a point where they can affect vampires.<br /> <br /> - Some mystical properties of vitae (bonding, ghouling, light Discipline effects) can be propagated through fruit of the plants. Commonly, the ratio invested to effectiveness is increased that way.<br /> <br /> - Plants change their morphology to reflect the vitae donor\u2019s Disciplines. Potence makes them huge, Obtenebration gloomy. Would be interesting to see a garden with one of the more exotic Disciplines.<br /> <br /> For interested PCs, I would realize this through a new Knowledge Ability (<b>Blood Gardening</b>), rather than a dedicated power. It\u2019s not exactly blood sorcery, rather limited in scope, and seems to be practiced throughout all kinds of Clans and Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Have you used Blood Gardens in your chronicle? I\u2019m curious to see what others have done with the idea.<br /> <br /> Also, if I missed out on important examples, let me know.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, there are plenty of examples of real world deadly &quot;Necro&quot; gardens. The The Alnwick Garden would be an easy example, imagine feeding it vitae to boost its deadly nature. then start looking at things like strangler figs, mind controlling cordycep mushrooms, mind altering vitae infused psilocybe mushrooms that could move characters between worlds, and so many more things that could be juiced up by vitae. Hell, you could even give the &quot;garden&quot; different abilities depending on what clan is feeding it so different clans could theoretically have the same gardens with different abilities and uses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T16:51:15-07:00","id":1515801,"title":"","content":"I once played a Telyav whose primary path was Spirit Manipulation, and her three secondary paths were Green Path, Neptune's Might, and Rego Mentem (i.e. spirit summoning). Green Path was <i>by far</i> the MVP in that path lineup, especially when it turned out the Keeper of Elysium was a real plant lover who kept potted plants and flowers in court and every side room. That character's information brokering put the Nosferatu to shame, and the one time her haven was attacked, it <i>did not</i> end well for the perpetrator.<br /> <br /> But the most fun part of that character was leaving everyone wondering if my character was a Toreador or a Malkavian. That's what tends to happen, when you're known for conversing with plants and toilets more than other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T07:06:26-07:00","id":1515860,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I forgot to put in Green Path and Sielanic Thauma. I had those on my list, and then simply forgot to include them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515762#post1515762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Undead' gardens sends really the wrong message. A dead plant can't be more valuable than a live plant, and it's quite the masquerade breach. There are going to be special vampire gardens, but I think you're being too optimistic with the extent. The canabis used for Kalif isn't going to come across as anything more than an impressive strain to most experts, it won't shatter the masquerade, but an undead plant would cause some problems.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. I would edit the first post, but don't want to trip the spam filter. The books use 'ghouled'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515762#post1515762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyss mysticism certainly won't be good for plants, the abyss is hostile to all life, but I think I did read somewhere that the bahari believe that Tzmisce and Lasombra got their signature powers by raiding lilith's garden, so maybe there's something there. Whatever it is, it's an abomination that should magnetize hunters to it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will have to look that Bahari bit up, that sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515762#post1515762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The further a species is away from human, the less magical and the more physical the alterations will get. Humans don't physically change at all, Horses or dogs on Vitae will look like they're on Trenbolone, rats will double their mass while fingernail-sized spiders will grow a hundred fold o palm-sized. Animals strictly have discipline limitations and can never learn things like Obtenebration (or protean, which I think is stupid, because it was made for them, but anyhow) With that in mind, I think plants will absorb vitae with extreme inefficiency and the donor's disciplines won't give them anything special.</div> </div> </div> </div> The connection between changes in appearance and Disciplines are directly extrapolated from the examples in the books, ie Nosferatu shrooms are giants, de Flores' plants &quot;show death-pale tints or dark, Abyss-tainted hues, and a few masterpieces display unusual powers of their own&quot;, and for Vicissitude &quot;take on a reddish hue and manifest elements of [the Asakku's] Vicissitude, warping and twisting in alien fashion&quot;. Beyond that, I would give plants only hints of the Disciplines, never a full dot. Slightly ghostly for Necromancy, easy to miss for Obfuscate, extremely territorial for Dominate etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515765#post1515765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During one Tremere centric game we used the Green Path to build living focal points on top of ley lines and such. The trees and plants were both laid out in arcane patterns and were chosen for their occult meaning. The plants were then treated with alchemical catalysts to promote magical conductivity. Copious amounts of vitae were also poured over the plants to ensure their proper attunement to thaumaturgical processes. It's not a blood garden per se, but it allowed for some nice house rule bonuses for casting rituals and what not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea for the 'telluric' use. Was this DA or modern setting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515796#post1515796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, there are plenty of examples of real world deadly &quot;Necro&quot; gardens. The Alnwick Garden would be an easy example</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe city I live in has a botanical garden with many exotic plants, and it overlaps with an archeological dig site for bronze age burial mounds. If I were a Necromancer with a green thumb, I would totally nab that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515801#post1515801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one time her haven was attacked, it <i>did not</i> end well for the perpetrator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you have a description for the Haven? What kind of plants did she use for defense?<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T07:07:37-07:00","id":1515861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515796#post1515796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this, there are plenty of examples of real world deadly &quot;Necro&quot; gardens. The The Alnwick Garden would be an easy example, imagine feeding it vitae to boost its deadly nature. then start looking at things like strangler figs, mind controlling cordycep mushrooms, mind altering vitae infused psilocybe mushrooms that could move characters between worlds, and so many more things that could be juiced up by vitae. Hell, you could even give the &quot;garden&quot; different abilities depending on what clan is feeding it so different clans could theoretically have the same gardens with different abilities and uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>so playing off this idea a little more, you could have the clan disciplines be the inspiration for whatever traits the necro garden has","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T07:20:02-07:00","id":1515862,"title":"","content":"All the vampire pumpkins and watermelons had to come from somewhere\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> For some reason I have this mental image of the stake of a staked elder in torpor growing back into a full tree, then a copse of trees, then a small forest. The plants work to keep the torpid elder safe and fed; destroy the flora, and either the elder starves or rises pissed off.<br /> <br /> Protean users could learn to sink into trees instead of earth. Maybe some unique ghouls and revenants learn to do that. I think there was something similar in Requiem, though I can\u2019t recall it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T07:59:01-07:00","id":1515865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515861#post1515861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so playing off this idea a little more, you could have the clan disciplines be the inspiration for whatever traits the necro garden has</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, there are some fun options:<br /> - The whispering gardens of a Daughter's Melpominee<br /> - The enchanted grove of a Kiasyd<br /> - The eerie copse of a circle of Bloodbrother groundskeepers<br /> - The maddening hedge maze of a Malkavian<br /> etc etc<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515862#post1515862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason I have this mental image of the stake of a staked elder in torpor growing back into a full tree, then a copse of trees, then a small forest. The plants work to keep the torpid elder safe and fed; destroy the flora, and either the elder starves or rises pissed off.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b This is very close to my head-canon how some Lhiannan elders could have made it into modern times.<br /> Could also double as a torture if the enclosed vampire is conscious, immobile but never in Torpor. Sounds like a level 5 Ritual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515862#post1515862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protean users could learn to sink into trees instead of earth. Maybe some unique ghouls and revenants learn to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's at least a power in Sielanic Thaumaturgy. I also thought about Vicissitude being able to manipulate plant matter; if the.. states.. of the Eldest are any indication, the potential to affect non-flesh matter is at least theoretically there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T08:42:00-07:00","id":1515869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515865#post1515865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYeah, there are some fun options:<br /> - The whispering gardens of a Daughter's Melpominee<br /> - The enchanted grove of a Kiasyd<br /> - The eerie copse of a circle of Bloodbrother groundskeepers<br /> - The maddening hedge maze of a Malkavian<br /> etc etc<br /> <br /> \u200b This is very close to my head-canon how some Lhiannan elders could have made it into modern times.<br /> Could also double as a torture if the enclosed vampire is conscious, immobile but never in Torpor. Sounds like a level 5 Ritual.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's at least a power in Sielanic Thaumaturgy. I also thought about Vicissitude being able to manipulate plant matter; if the.. states.. of the Eldest are any indication, the potential to affect non-flesh matter is at least theoretically there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't even thinking about making the garden that thematic but I like your line of thinking more than I did mine, I was thinking something like say a malk maintaining a garden would create incredibly hallucinogenic properties and possibly allow someone to punch through the film between dimensions and make it into the umbra or some other realm of existence but having a garden maze that will induce insanity or clarity depending on your point of view and still possibly be a way to punch a hole into other realms is an even better idea or a Kiasyd garden that eventually turns into the dreaming and ultimately leads to the Wyld<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":359,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","user":"Dezeroth","date":". 06-22-2023, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T09:07:06-07:00","id":1515870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515862#post1515862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the vampire pumpkins and watermelons had to come from somewhere\u2026\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun, but &quot;true&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Vampire pumpkins and watermelons are a folk legend (mostly Romani Mythology) from the Balkans, in southeastern Europe<br /> The belief in vampire fruit is similar to the belief that any inanimate object left outside during the night of a full moon will become a vampire. One of the main indications that a pumpkin or melon is about to undergo a vampiric transformation (or has just completed one) is said to be the appearance of a drop of blood on its skin.<br /> According the Serbian ethnologist Tatomir Vukanovi\u0107, the transformation takes place if these fruits are kept for more than 10 days; at that point the pumpkins / watermelons gather and start to shake each other, making sounds like \u201cbrrrl, brrrl\u201d. At this point they would move around the houses trying to harm people ( Vukanovi\u0107 isn't clear on what sort of harm, but he does state that most people weren't afraid of these Dracula-esque fruits [Perkovski]. Perhaps it's because these watermelon and pumpkin vampires have no teeth, or that you could probably give it a good, swift kick and then make your escape....), but the people do not particularly fear them because they know that the damage they can receive is relative.<br /> To defeat them, it would be enough to boil and reduce them to a pulp, then sweep the remains with a broom and burn the latter; according to some particular traditions, pumpkins kept after Christmas would become vampires.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T10:32:19-07:00","id":1515875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1515860#post1515860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea for the 'telluric' use. Was this DA or modern setting?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a modern setting game; the coterie was tasked with building infrastructure for the clan. Each Chantry or focus project had a different theme and design requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T01:43:57-07:00","id":1515994,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of ghoul gardens and even revenant animals as set pieces.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s some SV books for V5 and Changeling which we use, the concept of cultivating ghoul breeds of fruit trees, roses etc in my mind is definitely in the realms of the Ventrue and Toreador as well as the fungi gardens of the Nosferatu and the connection to nature from the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> With all of the centuries of research into thaumaturgy and blood alchemy, it stands to reason that some kindred would extend botanical/herbal research plus those that loved growing plants in their mortal lives would likely continue in undeath.<br /> <br /> It helps to expand the kindred beyond just hunting, politicking etc, did the Second City also have great gardens.<br /> <br /> The idea of certain plants being discipline orientated to the vitae they are grown in is interesting, as well as the defensive capabilities would be very attractive to the Camarilla finding low key (Masquerade friendly) deterrents and defences.<br /> <br /> In our 19th Century San Francisco, as a background piece one of the cities Camarilla Toreador has an extensive Blood Garden, as well as trying to understand the unique properties of the areas Redwoods (borrowed from V5 San Francisco by Night), she cultivates a range of ghoul plants as objects of unnatural beauty as well as gifting select cuttings to the Prince and his council to enhance and protect their havens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T07:11:04-07:00","id":1516334,"title":"","content":"There is one extreme fringe case of Necrobotany that I didn't mention, and it just occurred to me because I'm currently going through the Wraith material:<br /> <br /> Very rare instances of Shadowland flora exist, that is, literal ghost plants. A truly dedicated Necromancer could - with considerable effort - create a ghost garden that only exists beyond the Shroud.<br /> <br /> This would probably be mostly a vanity or prestige project, but also a wonder and magnet for Wraiths. I <i>could </i>see this as a one-of-a-kind place maintained by Cappadocians or Lamiae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T10:08:36-07:00","id":1516350,"title":"","content":"Anne of Lilies and her flowers or the Demon Lichen from Victorian Age Vapire Companion may also be added to this topic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T12:06:27-07:00","id":1516357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1516334#post1516334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one extreme fringe case of Necrobotany that I didn't mention, and it just occurred to me because I'm currently going through the Wraith material:<br /> <br /> Very rare instances of Shadowland flora exist, that is, literal ghost plants. A truly dedicated Necromancer could - with considerable effort - create a ghost garden that only exists beyond the Shroud.<br /> <br /> This would probably be mostly a vanity or prestige project, but also a wonder and magnet for Wraiths. I <i>could </i>see this as a one-of-a-kind place maintained by Cappadocians or Lamiae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theres quite a few plants or flowers directly associated with summoning or assisting the manifestation of the dead.<br /> <br /> Hags Taper, Wormwood, Yew (The Death Tree), Willow, Myrrh, Mandrake, the list goes on there are a lot of plants and flowers (Marigolds, Carmellions, Carnations - all grave offerings) that could be shadowland plants for such a garden. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T03:16:17-07:00","id":1516424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1516350#post1516350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anne of Lilies and her flowers or the Demon Lichen from Victorian Age Vapire Companion may also be added to this topic</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately I don't have the book and the wiki isn't very forthcoming. Could you give a brief summary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T06:20:14-07:00","id":1516449,"title":"","content":"Anne of Lilies is... something - it is up to the sotryteller what she is<br /> She was born as a mortal in 1852, as a daughter of a british merchant living in Hong Kong<br /> In 1874, Anne and her father went on business trip to the mainland, China, to secure new trade relations but what happened during the expedition is unknown; her father dissapeard and only Anne came back, without any visible change, unharmed and refused to tell anyone whats happened<br /> When few days later a birtish operative visited her, she presented him a deal: She will have the the full support of the Briths goverment in whatever endeavor it pleases her to undertake. In turn, she will provide them information regarding the Supernatural, detailed inteligence about basically anthing that might threaten the Empire. Finally, any atempt to violate her privacy and/or hinder her movement would prove to be costly in ways they would never undestand.<br /> To make her point, with a single word she took away the ability of the agent to use his lower body and manifested a lily from under her tounge and promised, if she not be given an affermative answer before the lily withered, she will eat his soul and make the offer to his sucessor.<br /> Her Majesty's agents gain a valuable and dangerous contact in the seemingly always twenty girl who have/had the bad habit to make demands when doing business, manifesting a lily and promise, if her demand won't be met, she will return to eat the soul<br /> The lilies are resilient, unaturally, lasting from a few days to three weeks<br /> Only one record exist when someone refused her demand. He was found dead, covered from beautifull lilies growing from his body... with sweet aroma of the flowers and the fresh earth with a bit cognitohazardous effect; only after leaving the area the horror hit the officer who found the body, untill then he even smelled the flowers, enjoyed the smell and their beautiy<br /> The flowers won't kill a vampire, but very uncomfortable, and even if bloodly uprooted from the body, they will regrow in a few minute, and by growing from eyes, mouth, would render the victim blind and mute.<br /> But good smelling<br /> No one found a &quot;cure&quot; to Anne of Lilies judegement so far<br /> <br /> The Demon Lichen grows under cities<br /> Fragile plant, ill-suited to survival it cannot derive sustenance from sunlight, water or from the soil.<br /> But it thrives... by feeding on living creatures.<br /> With its long tendrils from cracks on the wall or on the ground, from below it seek the warmth of living bodies. When someone comes near to them, they release a cloud of spores. Inhaling the spores causes the victim to fall in coma. Soon, sticky weblike material will burst out from the body attaching the body to the walls, the floor, furniture, anything really. When the &quot;cocooned&quot; victim comes contact with the tendrils of the Demon Lichen, connection formed and it slowly drains the fluids and nurisment to the body untill it consumes it totally, leaving only the clothes and jeweles and any foregin object behind...<br /> Colonies of the lichens could be huge, humongous under the cities and getting rid of it is very hard, only burning away the center, the source is the only sure way, and even then some parts could survive and regrow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-28-2023, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T06:37:39-07:00","id":1516452,"title":"","content":"Anne reminds me of the description of certain demons from folklore. Burmese iirc, but could also have been Chinese.<br /> In any case, I would put her flower power safely into the realm of proper sorcery or some kind of curse. It's a good one though, and could be a template for a similar Ritual.<br /> <br /> The Lichen honestly sounds like something the Nosferatu would be happy to employ for security, as long as it doesn't get out of control. But also not something from this side of the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the summaries!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T08:44:48-07:00","id":1517072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515736-necrobotany?p=1516452#post1516452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lichen honestly sounds like something the Nosferatu would be happy to employ for security, as long as it doesn't get out of control. But also not something from this side of the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is prime crossover territory, one of the interesting things around Vampire in relation to other splats is that certain disciplines, rituals or even vitae may have effects that the kindred themselves are completely unaware of.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu breeding pools and even ghoul lichens as you say may have characteristics in the Shadowlands, Middle Umbra or even Dreaming that the vampires didn\u2019t intend but adds great props and atmosphere to say a warren even if sticking with pure VTM but adding a little other lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T19:22:37-07:00","id":1517129,"title":"","content":"Ghouled gardens are a thing in Requiem, or at least the first edition of Requiem. They were a big deal to the Circle of the Crone and their old Covenant book could have some useful info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-03-2023, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T05:58:11-07:00","id":1518636,"title":"","content":"A quick note to add to plant related powers because I just stumbled upon it, <i>Hands of Destruction </i>is a very easy reskin if you're looking for some Fungimancy. Just add some fungal growth as flair to the powers. Or maybe a sprout of Lilies if you prefer flowers, or thorns if you are Bahari.<br /> <br /> As an aside, that Path works thematically better as Necromancy, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-23-2023, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T18:17:20-07:00","id":1522681,"title":"","content":"While not being able to offer much to the conversation, I just wanted to remark on how fascinating this is and it's inspired me to look into adding such details to my own narratives. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26060-nuhxnger36","name":"NuHxnger36","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T08:17:36-07:00","id":1533380,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the bump, but I wanted to add the Bia\u0142owie\u017ca Kraina (VDA20: Tome of Secrets p.46) to the list of related powers. Koldunism mixes very well with Blood Gardening, given the Tzimisce's intimate relationship with their land. I'm surprised we don't see it mentioned within the Old Clan, it's a really good fit. The Kraina seems to shortcut some of the effects that would be attainable with Blood Gardening and is very nice to create a 'Mansion in the Wood' type setting.<br /> <br /> The modern Ways of Koldunic Sorcery are modeled after the classical elements plus Spirit, but given that 'Wood' is one of the additional elements that appears in some schools of thought I don't think that a plant related Way would be out of the question. Maybe something to play around with - a young Tzimisce anarch using urban plant life to enforce their territory could be an interesting twist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}